-- title:
--   Orders of jmath̄ - a sum to ψ(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $N$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$ and $q \nmid N$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, with $q$ prime. Inside the Laurent series field $K((X))$ put $\bar\jmath =$ `jqModC K`, the series $X^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3$ times the inverse of the Dedekind eta unit, and let `jqNModC K N` be its image under the substitution $X \mapsto X^N$ (the ring homomorphism `qExpand K N`, obtained by multiplying exponents by $N$); the field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` is the intermediate field of $K((X))/K$ generated by these two elements. Assume that `jqNModC K N` is separable over the subfield generated by $\bar\jmath$ over $K$. Let $a \in K$, and let $T$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC K N` over $K$ — that is, of valuation subrings containing $K$, distinct from the whole field, and principal ideal rings — such that $T$ consists of exactly those places $w$ at which $\mathrm{ord}_w(\bar\jmath - a) > 0$, where $\bar\jmath$ is the element `jGeomGen K N` of `modularFunctionFieldC K N` and $\mathrm{ord}_w$ is minus the logarithm of the associated height-one adic valuation. Then $\sum_{w \in T} \mathrm{ord}_w(\bar\jmath - a) = \psi(N)$, where $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$, i.e. $N \prod_{p \mid N}(1 + 1/p)$.
--
--   This is the degree formula $\sum_w e_w f_w = [\bar F_N : K(\bar\jmath)] = \psi(N)$ for the covering of the $\bar\jmath$-line by the level-$N$ geometric modular function field in characteristic $q \nmid N$, the inertia degrees $f_w$ all being $1$ because $K$ is algebraically closed, so that the orders of vanishing of $\bar\jmath - a$ are exactly the ramification indices above the point $\bar\jmath = a$. It is used in the analysis of places of the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $q$ and their specialisations, and thence in the non-vanishing statements for mod $p$ forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_sum_ord_jGeomGen_sub_eq_dedekindPsi.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_CharLSpecialFibreLevelNDictionary

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
